      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "If the Generic rig used bone names for tracked joints and certain animations, it might be far easier to implement. Depends on how IK is applied to Generic rigs vs Humanoid inside Unity itself, too. Sure, if you were importing a rig that was not made for VRChat already, you'd have to rename the bones yourself, but that's a far cry better than having NO tracking, and importing anything other than a normal human model will have its share of extra work to be done, anyways.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
